The AI agent must exclusively use `cmake --build ./build` (with the current working directory set to the project root) to compile the project after source-only code modifications. Treat `./build` as the active build tree for the current checkout/worktree; another host, container, WSL, or OS development environment must use another worktree. Top-level repository scripts may be executed when they are within the current human authorization; inspect scripts first when their effects are unclear. Unless the human explicitly authorizes a bootstrap/configuration task in the current conversation, the agent must not reconfigure, clean, install, regenerate, delete, move, or recreate build/toolchain outputs, and must not edit or execute CMake/bootstrap/LLVM toolchain paths that can cause a full or partial rebootstrap. Adhere to this directive without exception to maintain build consistency and avoid unintended side effects.
